<http://data.silknow.org/event/3f58eb6e-e002-3b11-bd88-f0008ed25a56>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Note in register says: 'this jacket does not belong to the dress from Corinth, T.207-1922. See Baneki Museum, Hellenic National Costumes, P1.24 for illustration of the costume from Corinth. It is not altogether clear from the donor's letter whether the jacket as well as the dress was acquired in Corinth. The jacket, however, was of a type widely worn by the middle class women in Greece in the ninteenth century - see 424-1889.'\n\nGift of Mrs. Basil Lubbock. An extract from the donor's letter transcribed in the register says 'I have a very nice old Greek peasant's dress that I got in Corinth some years ago. I have also an old black velvet gouave (?unclear word) coat trimmed gold lace.'."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9b13cd3e-289a-3e45-bf25-bfe483645ce4> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Note in register says: 'this jacket does not belong to the dress from Corinth, T.207-1922. See Baneki Museum, Hellenic National Costumes, P1.24 for illustration of the costume from Corinth. It is not altogether clear from the donor's letter whether the jacket as well as the dress was acquired in Corinth. The jacket, however, was of a type widely worn by the middle class women in Greece in the ninteenth century - see 424-1889.'\n\nGift of Mrs. Basil Lubbock. An extract from the donor's letter transcribed in the register says 'I have a very nice old Greek peasant's dress that I got in Corinth some years ago. I have also an old black velvet gouave (?unclear word) coat trimmed gold lace.'."@en .

